{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Talking About the Future"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "That's Just Silly Talk"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. This is the past in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> tense, the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I will be studying at the library at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The person will start studying at some point in the future and be studying at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop studying. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the Future Perfect tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You can call me at work at 8 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have arrived</span> at the office by 8.  <br/>The train will leave the station at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the station at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the train <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> (<span class=\\\"italic\\\">not</span>) + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span> + verb <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span> you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">be heading</span> back to work tomorrow?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In five years, I<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'ll have saved</span> enough money to buy a house. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll have paid for almost half of the trip by the end of the month."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll have saved enough money to buy a house. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before that happens I'll have started my own PR company. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Will you be heading back to work tomorrow?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be blogging!"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Future Actions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong italic\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I will also stop squandering my money. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong italic\\\">Be going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Basically for the next two years I am going to spend as little money as possible.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Peter's picking us up soon. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It opens at 8:30.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am putting in at least 60 hours at the restaurant this week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will also stop squandering my money. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's going to be a challenge."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am starting a retirement fund as soon as I pay off the trip. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I meet with someone at the bank tomorrow work. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It opens at 8:30 and I have the first appointment."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You guys will be fine."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to keep up to date"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to provide the latest information to someone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I need you to keep me up to date while you're away. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you to talk about saving money for the future."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "safe and sound"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "free from danger or injury"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm back home safe and sound!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "elusive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "hard to understand"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You've been so elusive about your future. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reasonable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "fairly or moderately good"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That sounds reasonable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to keep an eye on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bwatch someone or something or \u200bstay \u200binformed about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to keep an eye on your money."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "returns"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the monetary benefits one gets back from investing their money"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I just hope I'm getting the best returns on my investments."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be ahead of the game"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have an advantage in a competitive situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're ahead of the game."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to squirrel away"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "save up for future use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have friends who have already squirreled away enough savings to retire! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le14ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le14ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of 12 questions to ask someone about her/his future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down the questions, making sure that you use various verb tenses (simple present, going to, present continuous, future continuous, future perfect and simple future)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find two people and ask them the questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes on their answers to each question."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think of and write down 12 questions about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask two people the questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes on their answers."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about jobs, work and money."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about future action. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "conte